  "published": "2025-08-31T20:12:45.453Z",
  "readmeFile": "docs\\readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 0.5.0 introduces a major refinement of the API for improved usability, clarity, and more powerful error handling.\n\n**New Error Handling System (Breaking Change):**\n- Error messages are now defined declaratively using one or more `[Error(key, message)]` attributes on the function class.\n- `EFIException` is now thrown using a short, user-defined string `key` instead of a numeric index.\n- The framework can now intercept a standard `System.Exception` and convert it into a custom Mathcad error.\n\n**API and Project Refinements (Breaking Change):**\n- The base class for functions has been renamed from `MathcadFunction` to the more intuitive `CustomFunction`.\n- Namespaces have been reorganized for clarity into `NetEFI.Runtime` and `NetEFI.Functions`. The old `NetEFI.Computables` and `NetEFI.Design` namespaces have been removed.\n- The low-level `IComputable` interface is now an internal implementation detail, hidden from the public API.\n- The C++/CLI host project and its output DLL have been renamed to `NetEFI` for consistency.\n\n**New Features:**\n- A new `context.Invoke<TResult>(...)` method allows for type-safe calls between custom functions.",
  "repository": "",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "title": "NetEFI Framework for Mathcad",
